{
  "abstract": "Unconditional Lean 4 + Mathlib formalization proving that no odd perfect number N = pi^alpha * q_1^(r-1) * ... * q_t^(r-1) has every non-special prime raised to the same exponent r - 1 for any odd prime 3 <= r <= 73 (all 20 odd primes, 1 <= beta <= 36 where r = 2*beta + 1), together with Kanold's theorem (notSpecial_of_prime) that r cannot be the special prime for any odd prime r >= 3. Independently proves the 9 classical prime cases in this range and settles all 11 remaining prime cases through r = 73 (including beta = 9, 15, 20, 21, 23 left open by Cohen and Williams 1985, plus r = 53, 59, 61, 67, 71, 73). Companion write-up, additional larger certificates through r = 167 (not packaged in this single repository due to certificate size), and dated literature search logs are published at https://mathdiscoveries.org/results/odd-perfect-equal-exponents.",
